---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
---
<ToolLayout
  slug="whois-lookup"
  title="WHOIS / RDAP Lookup"
  description="Look up a domain's registrar, expiry date, EPP status locks, nameservers and DNSSEC state over RDAP — the structured JSON protocol that replaced port-43 WHOIS."
  heading="WHOIS lookup, over RDAP"
  intro="Reads a domain's registration record straight from the registry's RDAP service and translates it into plain findings: who the registrar is, when it expires, and whether the transfer lock that stops hijacking is actually switched on."
>
  <div slot="input" class="wl-bar">
    <form id="wl-form" class="wl-form" novalidate>
      <label class="visually-hidden" for="wl-domain">Domain name to look up</label>
      <input
        id="wl-domain"
        name="domain"
        type="text"
        class="wl-input mono"
        placeholder="example.com"
        autocomplete="off"
        autocapitalize="off"
        spellcheck="false"
        enterkeyhint="go"
      />
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary" id="wl-go">Look up</button>
    </form>

    <div class="wl-examples">
      <span class="wl-examples-label">Try</span>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm mono" data-wl-example="icann.org">icann.org</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm mono" data-wl-example="cloudflare.com">cloudflare.com</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm mono" data-wl-example="worldlink.com.np">worldlink.com.np</button>
    </div>

    <p class="wl-hint">
      The query leaves your browser for <span class="mono">rdap.org</span>, which redirects it to the registry
      that runs the TLD. Both of them see the domain you typed. This site stores nothing and has no server in
      the path.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="section wl-sec">
    <div class="container">
      <div id="wl-out" class="wl-out" aria-live="polite">
        <div class="wl-card wl-idle">
          <h3 class="wl-card-title">Nothing looked up yet</h3>
          <p>
            Enter a domain above. You will get the registrar of record and its abuse contact, the registry's
            own dates, an expiry verdict, every EPP status code translated into what it actually does, the
            nameservers the registry has on file, and whether DNSSEC is signed at the parent.
          </p>
          <p class="wl-muted">
            Internationalised names must be entered in punycode — <span class="mono">xn--</span> form — because
            the RDAP bootstrap expects an LDH label.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wl-notes-sec">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Background</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Why registration data looks the way it does now</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Three things changed in the last decade: the protocol, the default security posture, and what a
          registry is legally allowed to publish. All three show up in the output above.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <article class="glass-card">
          <div class="icon-tile"><Icon name="code" size={20} /></div>
          <h3 class="h3">RDAP replaced port-43 WHOIS</h3>
          <p>
            Classic WHOIS was a 1982 design: open a TCP socket to port 43, send a bare domain name, get back
            free text. There was no schema, so every registry invented its own field names and date formats and
            every parser was a pile of regular expressions that broke whenever a registry restyled its output.
            There was no internationalisation, no authentication, and no way to ask for one specific object.
          </p>
          <p>
            RDAP (RFC 7480–7484, plus RFC 9082/9083) is the ICANN-mandated replacement: HTTPS, JSON with a
            defined vocabulary, UTF-8 throughout, and a bootstrap registry at IANA that maps every TLD to the
            server that answers for it. Because it is HTTP it can be cached, rate-limited per client, and — the
            part that matters most — <em>authenticated</em>, so a registry can show a verified law-enforcement
            or trademark requester more than it shows an anonymous one. That tiered access is the whole reason
            RDAP was pushed through, and it is why this page can exist at all: a browser cannot open a raw
            port-43 socket, but it can make a CORS-permitted HTTPS request.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="glass-card">
          <div class="icon-tile"><Icon name="shield" size={20} /></div>
          <h3 class="h3">The transfer lock is the real defence</h3>
          <p>
            Domain hijacking almost never involves breaking DNS. It involves getting the registration moved to
            a registrar the attacker controls — after that, they own the nameservers, the mail routing, and
            every password reset that depends on the domain. The standard route is an unauthorised transfer
            request: obtain the auth code or compromise the registrar account, submit the transfer, and wait.
            Under ICANN's transfer policy an unanswered request is <strong>auto-approved after five
            days</strong>, so silence works in the attacker's favour.
          </p>
          <p>
            <span class="mono">clientTransferProhibited</span> stops that at the registry: the transfer is
            refused outright until the lock is deliberately cleared from the owning account. It costs nothing,
            most registrars set it by default, and its absence — reported as <span class="mono">ok</span> with
            no locks — is one of the few genuinely actionable things public registration data still reveals.
            Pair it with <span class="mono">clientDeleteProhibited</span> so a delete cannot be issued either,
            and treat <span class="mono">clientUpdateProhibited</span> as a deliberate trade-off: it blocks
            unauthorised edits and your own emergency DNS change equally.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="glass-card">
          <div class="icon-tile"><Icon name="users" size={20} /></div>
          <h3 class="h3">Why the registrant is blank</h3>
          <p>
            Until 2018 a WHOIS record typically carried the registrant's name, postal address, phone number
            and email. GDPR made publishing that for a natural person unlawful without a basis, and ICANN's
            Temporary Specification — later the Registration Data Policy — told contracted registries and
            registrars to withhold most contact fields from anonymous queries. Registries outside the EU
            followed, because the data is global and the liability is not worth the transparency.
          </p>
          <p>
            So a redacted registrant is the expected output, not a failed lookup. RFC 9537 gives registries a
            way to say so explicitly, listing which fields were removed and why, and this tool reports that
            declaration when it is present. What survives is the registrar of record and its abuse contact,
            which is the useful part anyway: the registrar is who you file a transfer dispute, an abuse report
            or a data-disclosure request with. Named registrant details are still obtainable — through the
            registrar's disclosure process or ICANN's RDRS — just not from an anonymous request like this one.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="glass-card wl-limits">
        <div class="icon-tile"><Icon name="pulse" size={20} /></div>
        <h3 class="h3">What this tool cannot tell you</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>It only speaks RDAP.</strong> A browser cannot open a port-43 socket, so any registry that
            still publishes registration data only over legacy WHOIS returns nothing here. That is a gap in
            reach, not evidence about the domain.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Some TLDs run no RDAP service at all.</strong> <span class="mono">.np</span>,
            <span class="mono">.io</span> and <span class="mono">.bt</span> are examples. For those the page
            falls back to DNS delegation and says plainly that registration data is unavailable — it never
            infers "unregistered" from a missing service.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>DNS delegation is corroboration, not proof.</strong> A registered domain with no
            nameservers set looks identical, from outside, to one that was never registered.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>It never tells you a name is available to buy.</strong> Absence of a registry record does
            not account for reserved strings, premium tiers, registry policy or a pending application. Only a
            registrar's own availability check is authoritative.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>RDAP is rate-limited.</strong> A 429 or 503 is the service answering about itself, not
            about your domain. Errors of that kind are reported as service failures and no verdict is given.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>The data can lag.</strong> RDAP is served from the registry database, which trails
            registrar-side changes by minutes to a day. Where the registry publishes a "last update of RDAP
            database" timestamp it is shown, so you can see how stale the answer is.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>This is not a legal record.</strong> For a UDRP filing, a court production or anything
            evidentiary, obtain the registry's or registrar's own certified output.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ToolLayout>

<style>
  /* ---------------------------------- input --------------------------------- */
  .wl-bar {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.85rem;
  }

  .wl-form {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .wl-input {
    flex: 1 1 18rem;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text);
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    transition: border-color 0.18s var(--ease-out), background 0.18s var(--ease-out);
  }
  .wl-input::placeholder { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .wl-input:focus-visible {
    outline: none;
    border-color: var(--accent-blue);
    background: var(--surface-strong);
  }

  .wl-examples {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }
  .wl-examples-label {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .wl-hint {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  /* --------------------------------- output ---------------------------------
     Everything below `.wl-out` is written by JavaScript, so it never receives
     Astro's scope attribute — each descendant selector has to be :global(). */
  .wl-out {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .wl-out :global(.wl-card) {
    padding: 1.25rem 1.4rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-card > *) { margin-block: 0 0.7rem; }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-card > *:last-child) { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-card p) {
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-soft);
    max-width: 78ch;
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-card-title) {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-sub) {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-muted) { color: var(--text-muted) !important; font-size: 0.87rem !important; }

  /* headline card for the resolved domain */
  .wl-out :global(.wl-head) {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-head-name) {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 3.4vw, 1.5rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
    word-break: break-all;
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-head-tld) {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  /* key/value list */
  .wl-out :global(.wl-kv) {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(9rem, max-content) 1fr;
    gap: 0.15rem 1.1rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-kv > div) { display: contents; }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-kv dt) {
    padding: 0.42rem 0;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-kv dd) {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.42rem 0;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--text);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-kv > div:first-child dt),
  .wl-out :global(.wl-kv > div:first-child dd) { border-top: 0; }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-kv a) { color: var(--accent-blue); }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-age) { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.85em; }

  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    .wl-out :global(.wl-kv) { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0; }
    .wl-out :global(.wl-kv dt) { padding-bottom: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
    .wl-out :global(.wl-kv dd) { padding-top: 0.1rem; border-top: 0; }
    .wl-out :global(.wl-kv > div:first-child dd) { border-top: 0; }
  }

  /* findings */
  .wl-out :global(.wl-finds) {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.7rem;
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-find) {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left-width: 3px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--bg-elev);
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-find-body) { min-width: 0; }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-find h4) {
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    font-weight: 620;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-find p) {
    margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.62;
    color: var(--text-soft);
    max-width: 76ch;
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-find p:last-child) { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-fix) { color: var(--text) !important; }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-fix strong) { color: var(--accent-cyan); }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-epp) {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.1rem 0.45rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem !important;
    color: var(--text-muted) !important;
    background: var(--surface-strong);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
  }

  .wl-out :global(.wl-flag) {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    align-self: flex-start;
    min-width: 4.6rem;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-align: center;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    border: 1px solid currentColor;
  }

  .wl-out :global(.wl-find--pass) {
    border-left-color: var(--accent-cyan);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-cyan) 7%, var(--bg-elev));
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-find--pass .wl-flag) { color: var(--accent-cyan); }

  .wl-out :global(.wl-find--warn) {
    border-left-color: var(--accent-violet);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-violet) 8%, var(--bg-elev));
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-find--warn .wl-flag) { color: var(--accent-violet); }

  .wl-out :global(.wl-find--fail) {
    border-left-color: var(--accent-red);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-red) 9%, var(--bg-elev));
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-find--fail .wl-flag) { color: var(--accent-red); }

  .wl-out :global(.wl-find--unknown) {
    border-left-color: var(--border-strong);
    background: var(--bg-elev);
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-find--unknown .wl-flag) { color: var(--text-muted); }

  /* nameservers */
  .wl-out :global(.wl-ns) {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-ns li) {
    padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    color: var(--text);
    background: var(--surface-strong);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  /* provenance pane — fixed dark terminal palette, legible in both themes */
  .wl-out :global(.wl-term) {
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--term-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--term-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-term-bar) {
    padding: 0.45rem 0.85rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--term-accent);
    background: var(--term-bar);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--term-border);
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-term pre) {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.85rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--term-text);
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-term .t-cmd) { color: var(--term-cmd); }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-term .t-ok) { color: var(--term-ok); }

  /* status states */
  .wl-out :global(.wl-busy) {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-dots) {
    width: 0.9rem;
    height: 0.9rem;
    border: 2px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-top-color: var(--accent-blue);
    border-radius: 50%;
    animation: wl-spin 0.8s linear infinite;
  }
  @keyframes wl-spin { to { transform: rotate(360deg); } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .wl-out :global(.wl-dots) { animation-duration: 2.4s; }
  }

  .wl-out :global(.wl-err) {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-red) 45%, var(--border));
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-red) 8%, var(--surface));
  }
  .wl-out :global(.wl-err .wl-card-title) { color: var(--accent-red); }

  .wl-out :global(.wl-xlink) {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 550;
    color: var(--accent-blue);
  }

  /* -------------------------------- explainer ------------------------------- */
  .wl-notes-sec .glass-card p {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.68;
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }
  .wl-notes-sec .glass-card .mono { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text); }

  .wl-limits { margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .wl-limits ul {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }
  .wl-limits li {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-soft);
    max-width: 88ch;
  }
  .wl-limits li strong { color: var(--text); }
</style>

<script>
  import { lookupDomain } from '../../scripts/rdap-lookup.js';
  import { esc } from '../../scripts/tool-ui.js';

  const form = document.getElementById('wl-form');
  const input = document.getElementById('wl-domain');
  const btn = document.getElementById('wl-go');
  const out = document.getElementById('wl-out');

  if (form && input && btn && out) {
    const FLAG = { pass: 'Pass', warn: 'Check', fail: 'Act now', unknown: 'Unclear' };

    const sev = (s) => (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(FLAG, s) ? s : 'unknown');
    const iso = (d) => (d instanceof Date && !Number.isNaN(d.getTime()) ? d.toISOString().slice(0, 10) : '');

    /* EPP vocabulary is published as either "client transfer prohibited" or
       "clientTransferProhibited" depending on the registry, so compare on letters. */
    const key = (s) => String(s || '').toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z]/g, '');

    function yearsSince(d) {
      if (!(d instanceof Date)) return '';
      const y = (Date.now() - d.getTime()) / 31557600000;
      if (y < 1) return '';
      const n = Math.floor(y);
      return ` <span class="wl-age">(${n} year${n === 1 ? '' : 's'} ago)</span>`;
    }

    function card(title, bodyHtml, cls) {
      return `<div class="wl-card${cls ? ' ' + cls : ''}">
        ${title ? `<h3 class="wl-card-title">${esc(title)}</h3>` : ''}${bodyHtml}
      </div>`;
    }

    function finding(f) {
      const s = sev(f.status);
      return `<div class="wl-find wl-find--${s}">
        <span class="wl-flag">${FLAG[s]}</span>
        <div class="wl-find-body">
          <h4>${esc(f.title)}</h4>
          ${f.epp ? `<p class="wl-epp">${esc(f.epp)}</p>` : ''}
          <p>${esc(f.detail)}</p>
          ${f.fix ? `<p class="wl-fix"><strong>Do this:</strong> ${esc(f.fix)}</p>` : ''}
        </div>
      </div>`;
    }

    const finds = (list) => `<div class="wl-finds">${list.map(finding).join('')}</div>`;

    function row(k, valueHtml) {
      if (!valueHtml) return '';
      return `<div><dt>${esc(k)}</dt><dd>${valueHtml}</dd></div>`;
    }

    function provenance(domain, servedBy, status) {
      const code = status || 200;
      return `<div class="wl-term">
        <div class="wl-term-bar">rdap request</div>
        <pre><code><span class="t-cmd">GET</span> https://rdap.org/domain/${esc(domain)}
<span class="${code === 200 ? 't-ok' : 't-cmd'}">${code}</span> answered by ${esc(servedBy)}</code></pre>
      </div>`;
    }

    /* ------------------------------- kind: ok ------------------------------- */
    function renderOk(r) {
      const parts = [provenance(r.domain, r.servedBy)];

      parts.push(
        card(
          '',
          `<div class="wl-head">
            <span class="wl-head-name">${esc(r.domain)}</span>
            <span class="wl-head-tld">.${esc(r.tld)} &middot; registry data via ${esc(r.servedBy)}</span>
          </div>
          ${r.unicodeName ? `<p class="wl-muted">Unicode form: <span class="mono">${esc(r.unicodeName)}</span></p>` : ''}`
        )
      );

      /* --- registrar + dates --- */
      const reg = r.registrar;
      const rows = [
        row('Registrar', reg ? esc(reg.name) : '<span class="wl-age">Not published by this registry</span>'),
        reg && reg.ianaId ? row('IANA ID', `<span class="mono">${esc(reg.ianaId)}</span>`) : '',
        reg && reg.abuseEmail
          ? row('Abuse contact', `<a href="mailto:${esc(reg.abuseEmail)}" class="mono">${esc(reg.abuseEmail)}</a>`)
          : '',
        reg && reg.abuseTel ? row('Abuse phone', `<span class="mono">${esc(reg.abuseTel)}</span>`) : '',
        r.handle ? row('Registry handle', `<span class="mono">${esc(r.handle)}</span>`) : '',
        row(
          'Registered',
          iso(r.dates.registered)
            ? `<span class="mono">${iso(r.dates.registered)}</span>${yearsSince(r.dates.registered)}`
            : ''
        ),
        row('Registry expiry', iso(r.dates.expiry) ? `<span class="mono">${iso(r.dates.expiry)}</span>` : ''),
        row('Last changed', iso(r.dates.changed) ? `<span class="mono">${iso(r.dates.changed)}</span>` : ''),
        row('Last transferred', iso(r.dates.transferred) ? `<span class="mono">${iso(r.dates.transferred)}</span>` : ''),
        row('RDAP database updated', iso(r.dates.refreshed) ? `<span class="mono">${iso(r.dates.refreshed)}</span>` : ''),
      ]
        .filter(Boolean)
        .join('');

      parts.push(
        card(
          'Registration summary',
          `<dl class="wl-kv">${rows}</dl>
           <p class="wl-muted">Dates are the registry's own, in UTC. Blank fields are ones this registry does not publish over RDAP — not zeros.</p>`
        )
      );

      /* --- expiry --- */
      parts.push(card('Expiry', finds([r.expiryFinding])));

      /* --- hijacking locks, derived: absence of a lock is the finding --- */
      const codes = new Set((r.statuses || []).map((s) => key(s.code)));
      const has = (...k) => k.some((x) => codes.has(x));
      const locks = [];

      if (has('clienttransferprohibited', 'servertransferprohibited', 'transferprohibited')) {
        locks.push({
          status: 'pass',
          title: 'Transfer lock is set',
          detail:
            'A transfer to another registrar will be refused by the registry until the lock is deliberately removed. This is the single most effective protection against domain hijacking, because a hijack is almost always an unauthorised transfer rather than a DNS break.',
        });
      } else {
        locks.push({
          status: 'warn',
          title: 'No transfer lock on this domain',
          detail:
            'The registry published no transfer-prohibited status, so nothing at the registry is standing between this name and a transfer request. ICANN policy auto-approves an unanswered transfer after five days, so an attacker who obtains the auth code only needs the owner not to be paying attention.',
          fix: 'Turn on the registrar lock (clientTransferProhibited) in the registrar control panel — it is free, takes one click, and only needs clearing for the few minutes of a genuine transfer.',
        });
      }

      if (has('clientdeleteprohibited', 'serverdeleteprohibited', 'deleteprohibited')) {
        locks.push({
          status: 'pass',
          title: 'Deletion lock is set',
          detail:
            'A delete request for this domain will be rejected, so neither an accidental cancellation nor a malicious one takes effect while the lock stands.',
        });
      } else {
        locks.push({
          status: 'warn',
          title: 'No deletion lock on this domain',
          detail:
            'No delete-prohibited status is published. Deletion is the one domain mistake with a hard deadline attached: after the delete, restoration is a 30-day redemption window at several times the renewal fee, then the name drops to general availability.',
          fix: 'Enable clientDeleteProhibited alongside the transfer lock. Both are registrar-side switches on the same page.',
        });
      }

      parts.push(
        card(
          'Hijacking protections',
          `${finds(locks)}
           <p class="wl-muted">These two are derived from the status codes below: a lock that is absent publishes nothing, so its absence has to be read rather than reported.</p>`
        )
      );

      /* --- every published status --- */
      if (r.statuses && r.statuses.length) {
        parts.push(
          card(
            `Registry status codes (${r.statuses.length})`,
            `${finds(r.statuses)}
             <p class="wl-muted">EPP status codes are the registry's authoritative account of what can and cannot happen to this domain right now. Codes prefixed <span class="mono">client</span> were set by the registrar and can be cleared from your account; <span class="mono">server</span> codes are set at the registry and your registrar cannot lift them.</p>`
          )
        );
      } else {
        parts.push(
          card(
            'Registry status codes',
            `<p>This registry published no status codes at all in its RDAP response. That is a gap in the response rather than a clean bill of health — with no codes present, whether a transfer lock exists cannot be determined from here. Check the domain in your registrar control panel.</p>`
          )
        );
      }

      /* --- delegation + DNSSEC --- */
      const nsHtml = r.nameservers && r.nameservers.length
        ? `<ul class="wl-ns">${r.nameservers.map((n) => `<li>${esc(n)}</li>`).join('')}</ul>
           <p class="wl-muted">These are the nameservers recorded <em>at the registry</em>, which is what the delegation in the parent zone is built from. If they disagree with what your DNS provider shows, the registry wins.</p>`
        : `<p>The registry has no nameservers on file for this domain, so nothing about it resolves — no website, no mail. That is normal for a name held in reserve and a live outage for one that is meant to be in service.</p>`;

      parts.push(card('Nameservers at the registry', nsHtml));
      parts.push(card('DNSSEC', finds([r.dnssec])));

      /* --- registrant disclosure --- */
      let disclosure;
      if (r.contacts && r.contacts.length) {
        const rows2 = r.contacts
          .map((c) => {
            const bits = [c.org, c.name, c.email, c.tel, c.address].filter(Boolean).map(esc).join(' &middot; ');
            return row(c.role.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + c.role.slice(1), bits);
          })
          .join('');
        disclosure = `<dl class="wl-kv">${rows2}</dl>
          <p class="wl-muted">This registry still discloses some contact fields to anonymous queries. Many do not.</p>`;
      } else if (r.declaresRedaction) {
        disclosure = `<p>The registry <strong>explicitly declared this response redacted</strong> (RFC 9537), meaning registrant, admin and technical contact details were deliberately withheld from an anonymous query — the standard consequence of GDPR and ICANN's Registration Data Policy. This is expected output, not a failed lookup or a misconfigured domain.</p>
          <p>The registrar of record and its abuse contact above are the parts that remain, and they are the parts you actually need: transfer disputes, abuse reports and formal disclosure requests all go through the registrar. Named registrant details are still obtainable through the registrar's disclosure process or ICANN's RDRS, with a stated lawful basis.</p>`;
      } else {
        disclosure = `<p>No registrant, admin or technical contact details were published in this response, and the registry did not attach an explicit redaction declaration. In practice that is the same outcome as a declared redaction — almost every registry now withholds contact data from anonymous RDAP queries — it simply was not labelled as such. Do not read it as the domain having no registrant on file.</p>`;
      }
      parts.push(card('Registrant contact disclosure', disclosure));

      out.innerHTML = parts.join('');
    }

    /* ---------------------- DNS fallback narration (shared) ------------------ */
    function dnsBlock(dns, domain) {
      const state = dns && dns.state;

      if (state === 'delegated') {
        return `<p><strong>DNS says this name is in use.</strong> The parent zone delegates
          <span class="mono">${esc(domain)}</span> to the nameservers below, which only happens when a
          registration exists.</p>
          <ul class="wl-ns">${dns.nameservers.map((n) => `<li>${esc(n)}</li>`).join('')}</ul>`;
      }
      if (state === 'nxdomain') {
        return `<p><strong>DNS returns NXDOMAIN.</strong> No delegation for
          <span class="mono">${esc(domain)}</span> exists anywhere in the chain from the root. That is
          consistent with the name being unregistered, but it is not proof: a registered domain whose owner
          never set nameservers produces exactly the same answer.</p>`;
      }
      if (state === 'noanswer') {
        return `<p><strong>DNS resolved the name but returned no NS records.</strong> The name is known to the
          chain without a delegation of its own — typical of a registration held without nameservers, or of a
          label served from the parent zone. Inconclusive either way.</p>`;
      }
      return `<p><strong>The DNS cross-check failed as well.</strong> The DNS-over-HTTPS query could not be
        completed, usually because a network filter, extension or captive portal is blocking it. No conclusion
        can be drawn about this domain from here.</p>`;
    }

    const npLink = (tld) =>
      tld === 'np'
        ? `<p><a class="wl-xlink" href="/tools/np-domain-check">Use the .np domain check instead &rarr;</a>
           It works the way .np actually has to be checked — Mercantile's register is the only source of truth
           for that TLD, and no RDAP or WHOIS endpoint fronts it.</p>`
        : '';

    /* ---------------------------- kind: no-rdap ----------------------------- */
    function renderNoRdap(r) {
      out.innerHTML = card(
        `No RDAP service exists for .${r.tld}`,
        `<p>The bootstrap redirector at <span class="mono">rdap.org</span> answered directly rather than
          forwarding the query, which means the registry for <span class="mono">.${esc(r.tld)}</span> publishes
          no RDAP endpoint in IANA's bootstrap file. Nothing was asked of the registry, so
          <strong>nothing is known here about whether ${esc(r.domain)} is registered</strong>. This is a gap in
          the TLD's infrastructure, not a verdict on the domain.</p>
        <p class="wl-muted">Several ccTLDs are in this position — <span class="mono">.np</span>,
          <span class="mono">.io</span> and <span class="mono">.bt</span> among them. Some of them still run a
          port-43 WHOIS server or a web form, neither of which a browser can reach: port 43 is a raw socket, and
          web forms are same-origin only. Registration data for these TLDs has to come from the registry's own
          site.</p>
        ${npLink(r.tld)}
        <h3 class="wl-card-title">DNS delegation, as a fallback</h3>
        ${dnsBlock(r.dns, r.domain)}`,
        'wl-fallback'
      );
    }

    /* --------------------------- kind: not-found ---------------------------- */
    function renderNotFound(r) {
      const delegated = r.dns && r.dns.state === 'delegated';

      out.innerHTML =
        provenance(r.domain, r.servedBy, 404) +
        card(
          delegated
            ? `The registry has no record — but DNS disagrees`
            : `No registration record for ${r.domain}`,
          `<p>The query was redirected to <span class="mono">${esc(r.servedBy)}</span>, the registry's own RDAP
            service for <span class="mono">.${esc(r.tld)}</span>, and that service returned 404 for
            <span class="mono">${esc(r.domain)}</span>. Unlike a missing RDAP endpoint, this is a real answer
            from the authoritative source: it holds no registration object under that name.</p>
          ${
            delegated
              ? `<p><strong>Treat this as inconclusive, not as availability.</strong> A live delegation with no
                 registry record usually means one of three things: the RDAP service is lagging a very recent
                 registration, the name is a second-level label under a public suffix that the registry does not
                 expose as an object, or the RDAP object is filtered from anonymous queries. Verify with a
                 registrar before assuming anything.</p>`
              : `<p><strong>This is not the same as "available to buy."</strong> Reserved and blocked strings,
                 premium tiers, registry policy and pending applications all produce a missing record too. A
                 registrar's availability check is the only authoritative answer on whether you can register
                 it.</p>`
          }
          ${npLink(r.tld)}
          <h3 class="wl-card-title">DNS cross-check</h3>
          ${dnsBlock(r.dns, r.domain)}`,
          'wl-fallback'
        );
    }

    /* -------------------------------- runner -------------------------------- */
    function busy(domain) {
      out.innerHTML = card(
        '',
        `<div class="wl-busy"><span class="wl-dots" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>Querying RDAP for <span class="mono">${esc(domain)}</span>&hellip;</span></div>`
      );
    }

    function fail(message) {
      out.innerHTML = card(
        'Lookup did not complete',
        `<p>${esc(message)}</p>
         <p class="wl-muted">Nothing above should be read as information about the domain — a failed request
          says nothing about a registration either way.</p>`,
        'wl-err'
      );
    }

    let running = false;

    async function run(raw) {
      const typed = String(raw || '').trim();

      if (!typed) {
        fail('Enter a domain name first, for example example.com.');
        input.focus();
        return;
      }
      if (running) return;

      running = true;
      btn.disabled = true;
      busy(typed);

      try {
        const r = await lookupDomain(typed);

        if (r && r.kind === 'ok') renderOk(r);
        else if (r && r.kind === 'no-rdap') renderNoRdap(r);
        else if (r && r.kind === 'not-found') renderNotFound(r);
        else fail('The lookup returned a result shape this page does not recognise. Nothing can be concluded from it.');

        if (r && r.domain) {
          try {
            const u = new URL(window.location.href);
            u.searchParams.set('domain', r.domain);
            window.history.replaceState(null, '', u);
          } catch {
            /* a blocked history API must not lose the rendered result */
          }
        }
      } catch (err) {
        fail(
          (err && err.message) ||
            'The lookup failed for an unknown reason. Check the network connection and try again.'
        );
      } finally {
        running = false;
        btn.disabled = false;
      }
    }

    form.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      run(input.value);
    });

    for (const el of document.querySelectorAll('[data-wl-example]')) {
      el.addEventListener('click', () => {
        input.value = el.getAttribute('data-wl-example') || '';
        run(input.value);
      });
    }

    try {
      const q = new URL(window.location.href).searchParams.get('domain');
      if (q) {
        input.value = q;
        run(q);
      }
    } catch {
      /* deliberately silent: a malformed URL just means no prefill */
    }
  }
</script>
